"""fig3_3m_run_provenance.csv | main Fig. 3 (04_figures/fig.3/fig3_main_A4_v2.py)

Recovered statistical-analysis script | reproducibility package | Fig. 3 track.

WHAT THIS SCRIPT COMPUTES
    This code cross-checks reported 3M/268-parcel model results against a
    newer simulation run for a neuroscience manuscript's Figure 3. It
    computes a corrected NP-edge MSE value from Table S10 and compares it
    against the previously reported figure, and separately recomputes
    whole-brain functional connectivity correlations (per subject,
    averaged across the SST and MID task conditions using upper-triangle
    voxel-pair correlations) from a new run of the 3M model and compares
    the mean and standard deviation against the old run's values used in
    Table S9. One row of the output table represents one such comparison
    for a given panel and quantity, recording the old and new values,
    which version was actually used in the published figure, and whether
    the two runs agree or mismatch.

INPUT FILES
    Baseline_simulated_3m_task_FC.mat
    revision/10m_voxel_population_simulation/analysis_results/fc_similarity_four_runs_per_subject.csv
    simu_real_FC_across_scales_12subs.mat

OUTPUT FILE
    fig3_3m_run_provenance.csv
    written to OUT_DIR (default /tmp/recovery_scratch/fig3)
    reference copy in this package: 04_figures/fig.3/fig3_data/fig3_3m_run_provenance.csv

STATISTICAL TESTS
    descriptive summary only (no inferential test in the recovered cell)

RUNNABLE ON A LAPTOP
    no -- a name inherited from the session could not be recovered; see the NOT RECOVERED block

SEED
    not applicable (deterministic computation)

